# Kalsiyum

Unreal Engine 5, third-person action-adventure, PC only.
UE project root: `D:\Project Cal\Project_Calcium` (not `ue-project/`).
Campfire checkpoints (persistent world, Ghost of Tsushima style). Tone: sarcastic tragicomedy.
Story content is deferred — do not invent plot, dialogue trees, or the ending twist unless the user asks.

## Dual-AI

- You are usually the **polish / bug / feel** pass. Antigravity owns large scaffolds.
- Before editing, read `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` and `docs/SCOPE.md`.
- Do not rewrite systems another agent just scaffolded unless fixing a bug.
- End meaningful work by updating `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` (focus, owner, how to test).

## Agent stack (Cursor + Antigravity)

- **Superpowers:** brainstorm → plan → implement (TDD) → systematic-debug → verify before “done”.
- **Ponytail:** smallest complete change; prefer `/ponytail` on scaffolds and reviews.
- **Graphify:** if `graphify-out/graph.json` exists (repo root `Project Cal/`), answer architecture/relationship questions from the graph first (`/graphify query`).

## Scope

- v0.1 only: TP move + camera, melee, risky block → limb drop/reattach, 2 arm prosthetics, 3 flame moods, campfire save/rest, bone-density HUD, one blockout space.
- No roguelite runs, no first-person, no online, no seven culture kits yet.

## Code / content style

- Prefer Actor Components + DataAssets over a god Character Blueprint.
- Names: `BP_TP_Kalsiyum`, `BP_Campfire`, `AC_LimbSocket`, `AC_MoodFlame`, `DA_Limb_*`, `UI_BoneDensity`.
- Health is **Bone Density**.
- Camera: SpringArm follow; lock-on stub early, polish later.
- Placeholder meshes/anims OK; feel and rules first.
- Any player-facing text: short, sarcastic, not slapstick.

## Do not

- Add story systems “for later”
- Soften the block risk (block must be dangerous)
- Switch engine or to first-person without an explicit user decision
